From 46acc99953701dfd97bba6f4cdab2275a066cc03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:48:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] backends/monitor: Carry per-monitor target override
 declarations

Add MetaColorTargetOverride, a per-monitor declaration of an output's
target: an optional peak luminance, an optional black level and the
gamut source to use in BT.2100 (automatic, the base EDID colour
characteristics, or none). It is a user declaration, kept apart from
the encoding and from the colour device's own target selection.
Presence is explicit, because zero is a valid black level, and a
zero-initialized override declares nothing, so existing configurations
behave as before.

Carry the override from the monitor configuration through each output
assignment to the output, and expose it with
meta_monitor_get_color_target_override().

Link: TBD-MR
